# Tracer: replay exact complex algebraic normalization in Lean
#
# Before (did not work):
# 2 * i + 1 = i * i + 2 + 2 * i
# Former behavior: Litex rejected the equality, so no verifier-owned proof
# certificate could reach the compiler.
#
# Now (verified and compiled):
2 * i + 1 = i * i + 2 + 2 * i
(1 + i) * (1 - i) = 2
1 / i = -1 * i

forall z C:
    (z + i) * (z - i) = z * z + 1

# Current behavior: compiler validates ComplexAlgebraicNormalization evidence
# against the exact equality and emits a fixed native-complex proof adapter.
#
# Boundary: powers and symbolic denominators such as
# (z + i) / (z + i) remain fail-closed in this Lean adapter even when Litex
# verifies the source equality under a nonzero premise.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -strict -isolated -runner -f lean/examples/54_ComplexAlgebraicCalculation.lit
# Compiler: target/release/stmt_result_to_lean_compiler compile lean/examples/54_ComplexAlgebraicCalculation.lit
